  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @brief Processing function for Q15 normalized LMS filter.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[in] *S points to an instance of the Q15 normalized LMS filter structure.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[in] *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[in] *pRef points to the block of reference data.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[out] *pOut points to the block of output data.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[out] *pErr points to the block of error data.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @param[in] blockSize number of samples to process.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * @return none.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * The function is implemented using a 64-bit internal accumulator.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * Both coefficients and state variables are represented in 1.15 format and
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * multiplications yield a 2.30 result. The 2.30 intermediate results are
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * accumulated in a 64-bit accumulator in 34.30 format.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * There is no risk of internal overflow with this approach and the full
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * precision of intermediate multiplications is preserved. After all additions
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * have been performed, the accumulator is truncated to 34.15 format by
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * discarding low 15 bits. Lastly, the accumulator is saturated to yield a
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * result in 1.15 format.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * \par
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** * 	In this filter, filter coefficients are updated for each sample and the updation of filter coffi
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c **** *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q15.c ****  */
